  :notes
    "Sonnet distill chain auto-apply v1 is the FOURTH apply-gate landed in Wave 21, and the FIRST one whose `applied=true` outcome actually invokes a side-effecting LLM call. The earlier three gates (wave21-04 workstation LLM proposal v0; wave21-05 plan inference apply gate v1; wave21-06 LLM auto-approve proposal v0) are all conservative propose-only or pure deterministic-promote gates — they NEVER call Sonnet, only Sonnet's PROPOSALS surface. Wave21-07 introduces the first deliberate auto-INVOKE: when ALL six wave-20/06 deterministic safety rules pass, the wave-20 trigger has actually fired (auto_chain_trigger=auto_safe), the caller flips BOTH `auto_sonnet=true` AND `auto_sonnet_approved=true`, and the caller's `distill_mode` is NOT already sonnet, the daemon promotes the inner distill from dry_run to sonnet automatically and replaces the outer payload with the sonnet payload. This is the wave21-05 plan inference apply-gate pattern transplanted onto the wave-19/20 cross-plan distill chain: defaults stay off (byte-shape preserved); the apply path is gated on a deterministic safety inspector + an explicit caller approval flag; failures preserve the existing artifact verbatim. Conservative invariants I1-I7 (mirror wave21-04/05/06 patterns and mechanic.lisp's no-fallback principle from CLAUDE.md): (I1) DEFAULT `auto_sonnet=false` — existing callers see byte-identical wave-20 responses (no `auto_sonnet` block, no `auto_sonnet_status` shortcut). The fast-path early returns at the top of `maybe_apply_distill_chain_layers` cover three cases: trigger=Never+auto_chain=false+auto_sonnet=false (pure passthrough); trigger=Never+auto_chain=true+auto_sonnet=false (wave-19 only); trigger=auto_safe rules-failed+auto_sonnet=false (wave-20 trigger only). All three preserve their respective predecessor wave's byte-shape verbatim. (I2) NEVER auto-invoke Sonnet without BOTH `auto_sonnet=true` AND explicit `auto_sonnet_approved=true`. The latter is a SEPARATE caller-attestation flag — a single typo on EITHER cannot escalate the daemon. validate_auto_sonnet_args + plan.rs::validate_distill_chain_args reject string `\"true\"` and number `1` shapes with INVALID_PARAM at the action entry (defense-in-depth), and the read-side guards (auto_sonnet_requested / auto_sonnet_caller_approved) collapse non-bool / null / missing to false so a defensive accidental flip can never escalate either. (I3) NEVER auto-invoke Sonnet unless ALL six wave-20 deterministic safety rules pass. The auto-sonnet gate REUSES the trigger's rule outcomes verbatim via the AutoSonnetTriggerContext — it does not re-evaluate or relax them. Surface: when rules fail (rules_passed=false) the gate surfaces status=`skipped_rules_failed` with the trigger's full rule_value array. (I4) NEVER when caller's `distill_mode` was already `sonnet`. The caller already chose their mode; we refuse to double-invoke (would land a duplicate sidecar entry + burn tokens). The detector is case-sensitive on the literal lowercase `\"sonnet\"` so future-wave model variants (e.g. `\"sonnet-4.6\"`) will surface as `skipped_no_trigger`-equivalent rather than silently bypass — explicit refusal is preferred over guesswork. (I5) On Sonnet failure (handler error / structured error envelope / non-object payload) PRESERVE the existing inner payload. The auto-sonnet block surfaces status=`applied_sonnet` with model_call_status=`failed` (handler error) or `invalid_output` (structured error envelope from the sonnet path) and applied=false. The dry_run distill artifact (or the wave-19/20 chain receipts) on the inner payload stay durable — the operator sees both the failure diagnostic AND the original artifact, never just one. This is the CLAUDE.md `feedback_fail_fast_no_fallback` rule transplanted: we surface the failure loud rather than fall back to a degraded artifact. (I6) `review_required=true` PINNED on EVERY successful auto-sonnet outcome in v1. The auto-applied sonnet output is always receipt-only — no DB transition flips, the operator still reviews the distilled workflow before promoting. The sonnet payload itself already carries `review_required: true` for callers grepping that field directly; the auto_sonnet block makes it explicit on its own structured surface so dashboards have a single grep target. (I7) The wave-19 `auto_chain.status=\"recorded\"` and wave-20 `auto_trigger.trigger_status=\"triggered\"` blocks remain UNCHANGED — auto_sonnet is purely additive. When the auto-apply succeeds we carry forward `auto_chain` / `auto_chain_status` / `auto_chain_id` / `auto_trigger` / `auto_trigger_status` / `auto_trigger_chain_id` from the inner payload onto the new outer sonnet payload via a key-by-key splice (entry-or-insert so existing keys on the sonnet payload are NEVER overwritten). Wire shape: `auto_sonnet` block carries {requested (always true when surfaced), status (8-value enum), applied (bool — true only on `applied_sonnet` model_call_status=invoked path), review_required (always true — I6 pinned), model_call_status (4-value enum: not_invoked|invoked|failed|invalid_output), safety_rule_results (forwarded verbatim from trigger), caller_approval (echoes auto_sonnet_approved), caller_distill_mode? (echoes the user-supplied distill_mode), model_call_error? (stamped on failed/invalid_output), sidecar? (mirrors the trigger's sidecar path), chain_id? (mirrors auto_chain_id from wave-19 receipt)} + top-level shortcut `auto_sonnet_status` (matches the inner block's status). Sonnet sub-call argument synthesis: the gate clones args and flips `distill_mode=\"sonnet\"`, `auto_sonnet=false`, `auto_sonnet_approved=false`, `auto_chain=false`, `auto_chain_trigger=\"never\"` to prevent infinite recursion AND to prevent the sonnet sub-call from re-recording a chain entry (the parent already did). Direct call into action_distill_sonnet rather than action_distill so we bypass the top-level dispatcher's chain-orchestrator re-entry. plan.rs forwarding: apply_distill_chain unconditionally forwards auto_sonnet/auto_sonnet_approved/auto_chain_trigger/auto_trigger_min_evidence into the workflow.distill sub-call so plan-side callers (`mission_plan(...,distill_chain_mode=\"dry_run\",auto_sonnet=true,auto_sonnet_approved=true,auto_chain_trigger=\"auto_safe\")`) reach the same gate without re-shaping the arg envelope. plan.rs::validate_distill_chain_args adds defense-in-depth strict-shape validation (mirrors workflow::validate_auto_sonnet_args wording exactly via shared json_shape_label / shape_label helpers — both surfaces reject string `\"true\"` / number `1` with identical diagnostics so caller-facing error messages stay consistent across surfaces). MCP descriptor on workflow.rs gains `auto_sonnet` + `auto_sonnet_approved` properties with full invariant table I1-I7 in the English description + a bilingual paragraph in the Chinese tool-level description footer. Wave21-08+ hand-off: this gate's `applied=true` path is intentionally narrow (one caller approval flag, one trigger context, one upstream model). Future waves that want to layer additional auto-apply gates (e.g. methodology compile auto-promote, plan auto-finalize, retrospective auto-archive) should follow the same I1-I7 template — default off, dual opt-in (or stronger), reuse a deterministic safety inspector, preserve inner payload on failure, pin review_required=true in v1. The pattern is now four-deep (wave21-04/05/06/07) and stable enough to extract into a shared helper module in a future cleanup wave."
